on processes input with steps and returns results with premiums, which aligns with the name.\n\nDecision: Keep current name because it clearly reflects the function's purpose of calculating insurance premiums based on input items and processing fee.\n\n### Step 2: Calculate Initial APP Mass\n\n**Current Code Mass**:\n```typescript\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5; // G\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS = {\n  sword: 100, // G\n  amulet: 60, // G\n  staff: 80, // G\n  potion: 40, // G\n  rune: 25, // G\n  moonstone: 25 // G\n};\n\nconst calculateFinalPremium = (basePremium: number, processingFee: number): number => {\n  return Math.ceil(basePremium + processingFee);\n};\n\nexport const calculateInsurancePremium = (input: any): any => {\n  const results = [];\n  \n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      // Calculate base premium based on item types\n      let basePremium = 0;\n      for (const item of step.items) {\n        if (ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] !== undefined) {\n          basePremium += ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n        }\n      }\n      \n      // Calculate final premium with processing fee and rounding\n      const finalPremium = calculateFinalPremium(basePremium, PROCESSING_FEE);\n      results.push({ premium: finalPremium });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};\n```\n\nComponent Count:\n- Constants: 7 (PROCESSING_FEE, ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS object + 6 item values) = 7\n- Bindings: 6 (calculateFinalPremium, basePremium, item, step, results, input) = 6\n- Invocations: 5 (Math.ceil, +=, input.steps, step.items, results.push) = 10\n- Conditionals: 2 (if step.op === \"quote\", if ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type] !== undefined) = 8\n- Loops: 2 (for step of input.steps, for item of step.items) = 10\n- Assignments: 2 (basePremium = 0, results = []) = 12\n\nTotal Mass: 53\n\n### Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules (in order)\n\n#### Evaluate Rule 1: Tests Pass\n- All 6 tests are currently passing\n- 29 tests are skipped/todo (future f