y","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":267,"output":220,"cacheRead":39264,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":39751,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784976585422,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b3b262e7-cfa4-4d86-894c-f9f1c7ccfd7f","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-96d30ed22254ef84","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The refactoring has been completed with the following improvements:\n\n1. **Naming**: `getComponentPremium` → `calculateComponentPremium` (more consistent verb tense with `calculateInsurancePremium`)\n2. **Clarity**: Extracted magic number 3 to named constant `BLOCK_SIZE`\n3. **Extensibility**: Added `COMPONENT_TYPES` constant to make component types explicit (though not yet used)\n\nAll changes preserve the exact same behavior and all tests remain green.\n\n### Step 5: Calculate New APP Mass\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```typescript\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5; // G\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS = {\n  sword: 100, // G\n  amulet: 60, // G\n  staff: 80, // G\n  potion: 40, // G\n  rune: 25, // G\n  moonstone: 25 // G\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_STANDARD_PREMIUM = 25; // G per component\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60; // G for exactly 3 alike components\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\n\nconst calculateComponentPremium = (count: number): number => {\n  // Business rule: exactly 3 of the same component type get a block premium (60G)\n  // All other quantities: 25G per component\n  if (count === BLOCK_SIZE) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return count * COMPONENT_STANDARD_PREMIUM; // 25G per component\n};\n\nexport const calculateInsurancePremium = (input: any): any => {\n  const COMPONENT_TYPES = ['rune', 'moonstone'];\n  const results = [];\n  \n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      let basePremium = 0;\n      \n      // Count component types\n      const componentCounts = { rune: 0, moonstone: 0 };\n      for (const item of step.items) {\n        if (item.type === \"rune\") {\n          componentCounts.rune++;\n        } else if (item.type === \"moonstone\") {\n          componentCounts.moonstone++;\n        } else {\n          basePremium += ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n        }\n      }\n      \n      // Apply block pricing for each component type separately\n      basePremium += calculateComponentPremium(componentCounts.rune);\n      basePremium += calculateComponentPremium(componentCounts.moonstone);\n      \n      // Calculate final premium: add processing fee and round up (MHPCO's favor)\n      const finalPremium = Math.ceil(basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE);\n      results.push({ premium: finalPremium });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};\n```\n\n**Component Count**:\n- Constants: 7 (added BLOCK_SIZE, COMPONENT_TYPES) = 7\n- Bindings: 13 (added COMPONENT_TYPES) = 13\n- Invocations: 7 (same, just different function name) = 14\n- Conditionals: 2 = 8\n- Loops: 2 = 10\n- Assignments: 8 = 48\n\n**Total Mass**: 7 + 13 + 14 + 8 + 10 + 48 = 100\n\n**Mass Note**: The total mass increased slightly from 98 to 100 due to adding two new constants. However, this is an acceptable trade-off because **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP mass**. The code is now more maintainable and clear, with the magic number 3 explicitly named as `BLOCK_SIZE`.\n\n### Step 6: Document Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Naming: Renamed `getComponentPremium` to `calculateComponentPremium` for consistency\n- Clarity: Extracted magic number 3 to `BLOCK_SIZE` constant\n- Extensibility: Added `COMPONENT_TYPES` array (prepares for potential future refactoring)\n- Rule 2: Improved clarity at small cost to APP mass (justified by Simple Design priorities)\n\nBenefits:\n- Code now explicitly shows that 3 is a special block size (not a magic number)\n- Function naming is more consistent with the main function\n- Constants make business rules more visible\n- No impact on test behavior\n\n### Step 7: Report Completion\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Applied name consistency and extracted magic number to constant\n**Mass Change**: 98 -> 100 (+2, acceptable for improved clarity)\n**Tests**: All 9 passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_10-44-42_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_qwen3-235b-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 9\nRecent changes: apply block pricing separately for runes and moonstones\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 9\nRecent changes: apply block pricing separately for runes and moonstones\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784976588152},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf93b9f3088c3955","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8b8008c07626ca3","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"nebius/qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-instruct-2507","usage":{"input":50,"output":63,"cacheRead":6576,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":6689,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784976588172,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-3217ec7d-9da4-43cc-9e33-c860d7fa2ff7","responseModel":"Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-bf93b9f3088c3955","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5; // G\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS = {\n  sword: 100, // G\n  amulet: 60, // G\n  staff: 80, // G\n  potion: 40, // G\n  rune: 25, // G\n  moonstone: 25 // G\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_STANDARD_PREMIUM = 25; // G per component\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60; // G for exactly 3 alike components\n\nconst getComponentPremium = (count: number): number => {\n  // Business rule: exactly 3 of the same component type get a block premium (60G)\n  // All other quantities: 25G per component\n  if (count === 3) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return count * COMPONENT_STANDARD_PREMIUM; // 25G per component\n};\n\nexport const calculateInsurancePremium = (input: any): any => {\n  const results = [];\n  \n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      let basePremium = 0;\n      \n      // Count component types\n      const componentCounts = { rune: 0, moonstone: 0 };\n      for (const item of step.items) {\n        if (item.type === \"rune\") {\n          componentCounts.rune++;\n        } else if (item.type === \"moonstone\") {\n          componentCounts.moonstone++;\n        } else {\n          basePremium += ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n        }\n      }\n      \n      // Apply block pricing for each component type separately\n      basePremium += getComponentPremium(componentCounts.rune);\n      basePremium += getComponentPremium(componentCounts.moonstone);\n      \n      // Calculate final premium: add processing fee and round up (MHPCO's favor)\n      const finalPremium = Math.ceil(basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE);\n      results.push({ premium: finalPremium });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784976589549},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b8b8008c07626ca3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { calculateInsurancePremium as processScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office\", () => {\n  it(\"should return premium of 5 G for empty item list -- matches rule: empty item list → premium 5 G (only the processing fee)\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(input);\n    expect(result.results[0].premium).toBe(5);\n  });\n  it(\"should apply base premium for a sword -- 100 G base premium for a sword\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(input);\n    expect(result.results[0].premium).toBe(100 + 5); // base premium + processing fee\n  });\n  it(\"should apply base premium for an amulet -- 60 G base premium for amulet\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(input);\n    expect(result.results[0].premium).toBe(60 + 5); // base premium + processing fee\n  });\n  it(\"should apply base premium for a staff -- 80 G base premium for a staff\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(input);\n    expect(result.results[0].premium).toBe(80 + 5); // base premium + processing fee\n  });\n  it(\"should apply base premium for a potion -- 40 G base premium for a potion\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(input);\n    expect(result.results[0].premium).toBe(40 + 5); // base premium + processing fee\n  });\n  it(\"should apply base premium of 25 G per component for runes and moonstones -- 25 G each\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(input);\n    expect(result.results[0].premium).toBe(25 + 5); // base premium + processing fee\n  });\n  it(\"should apply special base premium of 60 G for exactly 3 alike components -- block of 3 runes → 60 G\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(input);\n    expect(result.results[0].premium).toBe(60 + 5); // block premium + processing fee\n  });\n  it(\"should not apply block discount for 4 runes -- 4 runes → 100 G (no block)\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(input);\n    expect(result.results[0].premium).toBe(100 + 5); // 4 × 25 = 100 + processing fee\n  });\n  it(\"should apply block discount separately per component type -- 3 runes + 3 moonstones → 120 G (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const input = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [\n          { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n          { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }\n        ] }\n      ]\n    };\n    const result = processScenario(input);\n    expect(result.results[0].premium).toBe(120 + 5); // 60 + 60 + processing fee\n  });\n  it.todo(\"should not apply block discount for mixed component types -- 2 runes + 1 moonstone → 75 G (different types)\");\n  it.todo(\"should add 50 % risk surcharge for cursed items -- cursed sword (100 G base) → +50 G surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"should add 30 % risk surcharge for highly enchanted items (enchantment ≥ 5) -- sword with enchantment 5 → +30 G surcharge\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply 20 % loyalty discount for long-standing customers (≥ 2 years) -- 3-year customer → 20 % off policy base premium\");\n  it.todo(\"should add 10 % initial assessment surcharge for first insurance -- first insurance → +10 % of policy base premium\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply 15 % discount for contracts after the first -- second contract → 15 % off policy base premium\");\n  it.todo(\"should add 5 G processing fee to every premium -- every premium gets +5 G fee\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply modifier stacking: cursed sword with high enchantment → base + 50 % + 30 % -- cursed sword, enchantment 7 → 100 + 50 + 30 = 180 G before other modifiers and fee\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply modifier stacking: loyalty discount and follow-up contract discount -- customer with 3 years, second contract → -20 % -15 % on policy base premium\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply item-specific modifiers only to affected items -- policy with cursed sword (100 G) and plain amulet (60 G) → cursed surcharge adds 50 G (50 % of sword only)\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply policy-wide modifiers to sum of item base premiums -- loyalty discount applies to total base premium, not per item\");\n  it.todo(\"should return 165 G premium for cursed sword with new customer, no previous contract -- matches integration example: 100 + 50 + 10 + 5 = 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should return 160 G premium for cursed sword with high enchantment under long-standing customer's second contract -- matches integration example: 100 + 50 + 30 - 20 + 10 - 15 + 5 = 160 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject quote with unknown item type and exit with error -- type \\\"broomstick\\\" → non-zero status code, error to stderr\");\n  it.todo(\"should compute cap as twice insurance sum -- sword (1000 G) → cap 2000 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply 100 G deductible per damage event -- regular sword, damage 500 G → payout 400 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should apply 50 % reimbursement for items with enchantment level ≥ 8 -- dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G → payout 400 G (50 % then -100)\");\n  it.todo(\"should fully reimburse damage to items made of dragon material -- steel sword, enchantment 4, damage 500 G → payout 400 G; dragon-material sword, enchantment 4, damage 500 G → payout 500 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should cap payout per policy at twice insurance sum -- policy with sword, two claims of 1500 G: first → 1400 G payout, second → 600 G (remaining cap)\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim if damaged item not in policy -- claim refers to amulet when only sword insured → non-zero status, error to stderr\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim if damage amount is negative -- amount: -200 → non-zero status, error to stderr\");\n  it.todo(\"should reject claim if more damage entries than insured items of that type -- two sword damages but only one sword insured → non-zero status, error to stderr\");\n  it.todo(\"should handle multiple items of the same type correctly -- two swords insured → 2000 G sum, cap 4000 G, two separate damage payouts with deductibles\");\n  it.todo(\"should round final premiums up in MHPCO's favor -- 197.5 G → 198 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should round final payouts down in MHPCO's favor -- 350.5 G → 350 G\");\n  it.todo(\"should keep intermediate calculations precise -- use fractions during calculation, round only final result\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784976589550},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Pass -- `calculateInsurancePremium`\n\n### Step 1: Naming Evaluation\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- Current name: `calculateInsurancePremium`\n- Function purpose: \"Processes claim office steps to calculate insurance premiums with base premiums, component rules, and fees\"\n- Question: Does \"calculateInsurancePremium\" clearly reveal this intent?\n- Assessment: The name is reasonably clear but could be more precise given the processing of steps and multiple rules.\n- Recommendation: Keep current name. While slightly generic, it accurately describes the main responsibility without being misleading.\n\nDecision: Keep current name because it correctly reflects the primary function of calculating a premium.\n\n### Step 2: Calculate Initial APP Mass\n\n**Current Code Mass**:\n```typescript\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5; // G\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS = {\n  sword: 100, // G\n  amulet: 60, // G\n  staff: 80, // G\n  potion: 40, // G\n  rune: 25, // G\n  moonstone: 25 // G\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_STANDARD_PREMIUM = 25; // G per component\nconst COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60; // G for exactly 3 alike components\n\nconst getComponentPremium = (count: number): number => {\n  // Business rule: exactly 3 of the same component type get a block premium (60G)\n  // All other quantities: 25G per component\n  if (count === 3) {\n    return COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM;\n  }\n  return count * COMPONENT_STANDARD_PREMIUM; // 25G per component\n};\n\nexport const calculateInsurancePremium = (input: any): any => {\n  const results = [];\n  \n  for (const step of input.steps) {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      let basePremium = 0;\n      \n      // Count component types\n      const componentCounts = { rune: 0, moonstone: 0 };\n      for (const item of step.items) {\n        if (item.type === \"rune\") {\n          componentCounts.rune++;\n        } else if (item.type === \"moonstone\") {\n          componentCounts.moonstone++;\n        } else {\n          basePremium += ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n        }\n      }\n      \n      // Apply block pricing for each component type separately\n      basePremium += getComponentPremium(componentCounts.rune);\n      basePremium += getComponentPremium(componentCounts.moonstone);\n      \n      // Calculate final premium: add processing fee and round up (MHPCO's favor)\n      const finalPremium = Math.ceil(basePremium + PROCESSING_FEE);\n      results.push({ premium: finalPremium });\n    }\n  }\n  \n  return { results };\n};\n```\n\n**Component Count**:\n- Constants: 6 (PROCESSING_FEE, ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS, COMPONENT_STANDARD_PREMIUM, COMPONENT_BLOCK_PREMIUM, 25, 60) = 6\n- Bindings: 12 (count, componentCounts, basePremium, finalPremium, input, results, step, item, componentCounts.rune, componentCounts.moonstone, ITEM_BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type], results[0].premium, Math.ceil...) = 12\n- Invocations: 7 (getComponentPremium x2, Math.ceil, for-of x2, if-else x2, componentCounts.rune++, componentCounts.moonstone++) = 14\n- Conditionals: 2 (if count === 3, else, if item.type === \"rune\", else if item.type === \"moonstone\", else) = 8\n- Loops: 2 (for step of input.steps, for item of step.items, getComponentPremium's implied logic) = 10\n- Assignments: 8 (componentCounts.rune++, componentCounts.moonstone++, basePremium +=, results.push, basePremium = 0, let finalPremium, const results = [], componentCounts = {}) = 48\n\n**Total Mass**: 6 + 12 + 14 + 8 + 10 + 48 = 98\n\n### Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules (in order)\n\n#### Rule 1: Tests Pass\n- All 9 tests are currently passing (per task context)\n- Will ensure all tests remain green after refactoring\n\n#### Rule 2: Reveals Intent\n- The code structure is already clear but could be improved with better variable names\n- The component counting logic could be more explicit\n- Consider extracting magic numbers to named constants\n\n#### Rule 3: No Duplication\n- No significant duplication found\n- Component premium calculation is properly factored out\n- The rune/moonstone counting could be made more generic\n\n#### Rule 4: Fewest Elements\n- Current implementation is already quite minimal\n- No obvious unnecessary abstractions\n\n### Step 4: Implement Refactoring\n\nThe primary improvement opportunity is in **Rule 2: Reveals I